# XCU gettext
# Copyright (c) 2026 Nicholas Martin. All rights reserved.
#
# no message catalogs are installed: TEXTDOMAINDIR points at an empty
# directory and LC_ALL is C, so the only observable result is the
# untranslated text (the msgid, or for ngettext the default singular or
# plural); translations are untestable portably because the locale names
# that select a catalog are not specified.

assertion  XCU.gettext.001
anchor     utilities/gettext.html#DESCRIPTION
anchor     utilities/gettext.html#OPERANDS
anchor     utilities/gettext.html#ENVIRONMENT VARIABLES
class      required
since      2024
says       With a text domain given as an operand, as -d, or in TEXTDOMAIN,
           and no catalog, the msgid is written to standard output unchanged
           and without a newline, with status 0.
test       t/001-domain-sources.sh

assertion  XCU.gettext.002
anchor     utilities/gettext.html#OPTIONS
anchor     utilities/gettext.html#DESCRIPTION
class      required
since      2024
says       -e processes C escape sequences in the msgid and -E leaves them
           as they are.
test       t/002-escapes.sh

assertion  XCU.gettext.003
anchor     utilities/gettext.html#OPTIONS
anchor     utilities/gettext.html#DESCRIPTION
class      required
since      2024
says       -s writes each msgid separated by a space and ends with a
           newline, -n omits that newline, and -E is the default with -s.
test       t/003-separate-s-n.sh
